description: Comment each function, each Quarto chunk, and each SQL query.
globs: "**/*.{py,qmd,sql}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Code comments

Comment the unit, not the line. One short sentence on what it does. Plain words. No comment that restates the next line.

## Functions

Put one `#` comment on the line above `def`. Say what the function returns or changes.

```python
# ❌ BAD
def money(x):
    # format x
    return f"${x:,.0f}"

# ✅ GOOD
# Format a dollar amount with no cents.
def money(x):
    return f"${x:,.0f}"
```

## Quarto chunks

One comment at the top of the chunk, after the `#|` options. That comment covers the chunk. Functions inside the chunk still get their own comment. Do not comment every line.

````
# ❌ BAD
```{python}
#| label: tbl-watch
# call md_table
# pass watch
md_table(watch)
```

# ✅ GOOD
```{python}
#| label: tbl-watch
# Show the watch list: the current count and when to act on it.
md_table(watch)
```
````

## SQL

One `--` line at the top of the file saying what the query returns. Do not comment each column.

```sql
-- ❌ BAD
SELECT COUNT(*) AS n  -- count the rows

-- ✅ GOOD
-- One row of headline counts: signups, buyers, spend, and the date problems.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS n
```

Skip generated files under `docs/` and `*_files/`.
